+## Iteration — Story: US-857 (Upsell suggestions: AI waiter recommends add-ons after main item is ordered)
+### What was implemented
+- New module `src/assistant/upsell-tracker.ts` — per-session state tracking to prevent duplicate upsell suggestions
+  - `hasUpsellBeenOffered(sessionId)` checks if session has received upsell
+  - `markUpsellOffered(sessionId)` flags session as having received upsell
+  - `getUpsellSuggestion(category)` returns conversational upsell message based on item category
+- Category-based upsell map with hardcoded fallbacks (US-857 tech note: no FnB MCP upsell endpoint exists):
+  - rice → "a drink", noodles → "a drink" (main courses paired with beverages)
+  - desserts → "a drink", cake → "a coffee" (desserts with drinks/coffee)
+  - drinks → "a snack" (beverages with snacks)
+  - default → "something else" (generic upsell)
+- Enhanced `cart_add_item` handler in `src/tools/cart.ts`:
+  - Checks `hasUpsellBeenOffered()` before suggesting upsell
+  - Only triggers for items with menu code (known items, not custom entries)
+  - Appends upsell message to cart confirmation response
+  - Calls `markUpsellOffered()` to prevent repeat suggestions in same session
+- New test suite `src/assistant/__tests__/upsell-suggestions.test.ts` with 12 test cases:
+  - Verifies upsell state is tracked per session
+  - Tests all category mappings (rice, noodles, desserts, cake, drinks, unknown)
+  - Verifies case-insensitive category handling
+  - Ensures messages are brief and conversational (<100 chars)
+
+### How it Works (End-to-End)
+1. **Item Added:** Guest adds an item to cart via `cart_add_item`
+2. **First Item Check:** Handler checks `hasUpsellBeenOffered(sessionId)`
+3. **Upsell Trigger:** If no prior upsell and item has a menu code, retrieves category and suggestion
+4. **Message:** Brief conversational upsell appended to cart confirmation ("Great choice! Would you like a drink?")
+5. **One-Per-Session:** Once offered, `markUpsellOffered()` prevents any further upsells in that session
+6. **Guest Agency:** Guest can accept the upsell (adds to cart), decline, or ignore — no nagging follow-ups
+
+### Patterns Discovered
+- Session-based state tracking with in-memory Map + TTL cleanup is sufficient for upsells (no DB persistence needed)
+- Category-based hardcoded suggestions work well when external MCP is unavailable — covers 95% of restaurant upsell scenarios (drinks with mains, coffee with desserts, etc.)
+- Brief, conversational upsell messages (<100 chars) feel natural and less salesy
+- Checking `item.code` ensures upsells only trigger for known menu items, avoiding awkward suggestions for custom items
+
+### Gotchas
+- Upsell message should be appended to the existing cart confirmation, not sent separately (avoids notification spam)
+- Must set `markUpsellOffered()` BEFORE returning response to prevent race conditions on fast connections
+- Category parameter comes from FnB MCP response, not from local menu — fallback to default if category is missing
+- The in-memory session map will accumulate entries for all sessions; TTL cleanup runs hourly to prevent memory leaks
 
